        "Abstract": "Understanding expressions that refer to the physical world is crucial for human-assisting systems. This paper proposes a multimodal reference resolution task and constructs a Japanese Conversation dataset for Real-world Reference Resolution (J-CRe3). The dataset contains egocentric video and dialogue audio of real-world conversations between two people acting as a master and an assistant robot at home. The dataset is annotated with crossmodal tags between phrases in the utterances and the object bounding boxes in the video frames."
